s3-5-p10 = prose (cons "Each clause named under composition is itself a term of the language, stated by the equations of this section and of CCHM [9]; it is not a rule of the net. Running a term is rewriting active pairs until none is left facing the place being read. Steps in different places touch different cells, so they proceed at once. A value is computed only as far as it is read. The foundation is visible in the rules: a cell has no content except which rules fire when something meets it; an open boundary is a free port, and a neutral is a cell waiting on one; every rule is one of the calculus's equations read from left to right, so a step never leaves the identity of the term it acts on; and univalence is the Glue rules, transport along the path of an equivalence ending at the equivalence's map applied. The rules above are those of the calculus. The machine has three further groups of operations, not listed here: arithmetic on words, machine-level values and bytes, and the operations by which the checker, itself a term, inspects values." nil)
